      "updated_at": "2022-08-16T10:22:13Z",
      "body": "Looked in to this a bit, and it seems like point #1 might not really be a thing? (If someone knows of a way, please correct me). I can't find a simple \"turn off tracking for the EU\" option for any of the analytics platforms with session recordings.\r\n\r\nBased (limited) understanding / reading of GDPR, this is because all the session recording tools use cookies (since that's literally what tracks the session) and under GDPR cookie IDs are considered personal data (this is the bit I'm most unclear about)\r\n\r\nIt also doesn't seem to work to just enable tracking by region/ geo (via ip range etc), because a) VPNs and b) GDPR applies to EU citizens even when they are abroad.\r\n\r\nBest I can tell, the only way to avoid the cookie popup / privacy policy is to not use cookies, eg using server-side tracking via api calls that do not include personal data, but this necessarily prevents us from (at least) the session replay requirement.\r\n",
